# UI and accessibility

Full direction in `docs/spec/01-design-system.md`. Read it before creating a component.
See `docs/spec/ADAPTATIONS.md` for stack path differences (Prisma, single app).

## The direction in one line

Turner & Townsend, clean blue and white: navy `#1e4479` brand, white surfaces, cool grey canvas,
generous spacing, clear hierarchy. Calm and confident enough to show a prospective client.
Build from `components/library` (see `50-ui-library.mdc` and `docs/redesign/README.md`).

## Non-negotiables

- **Tokens only.** Every colour comes from `styles/tokens.css` via the `asm-*` utilities. If a value
  you need doesn't exist, add a token. Never inline a hex value or use a raw Tailwind palette class.
- **Spacing** uses the Tailwind scale (multiples of 4px). No arbitrary pixel spacing.
- **Radius:** `rounded-asm` (10px) for controls, `rounded-asm-lg` (14px) for cards and panels,
  `rounded-full` for pills, badges, status and avatars.
- **No signal pink.** Emphasis is navy. Status uses the ok, warn and risk palettes only.
- **Every numeral is tabular.** `tabular-nums` on any score, count, measure or date.
- **Status renders glyph + label + wash.** Never colour alone.
- **A statutory gap is not an amber.** `<StatutoryFlag/>` stays visually distinct from `at-risk`.
- **`<TitleBlock/>` is the same component on screen and in the PDF cover.** Do not fork it.
- **Dark mode:** every library colour has an `html.dark` value. Check new screens in both themes.

## Accessibility — WCAG 2.2 AA is a release gate

- 4.5:1 body contrast, 3:1 large text and UI boundaries.
- 3px `--focus` outline with a 1px `--focus-shadow` inner ring. Never removed.
- 24×24px minimum target size.
- Every flow completable by keyboard. Org graph's accessible peer is `<OrgTable/>`.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` respected by chain rail, index delta and D3 force simulation.
- Visible persistent labels. Never placeholder-as-label.
- `lang` follows the EN/CY toggle.

Run axe-backed e2e before merging UI changes when practical.

## Component conventions

- Server components by default. `'use client'` only for graph, chain rail, forms, command palette.
- Product domain components live in `components/product/`.

## Motion budget

Hover and focus transitions on cards and buttons, the index delta and the chain rail slide.
Nothing else animates. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
